# /etc/lemnos/lemnos-orion.env: read by lemnos-orion.service and by S51lemnos-orion. Lines are
# shell-sourceable. Install as /etc/lemnos/lemnos-orion.env. See packaging/README.md, "The Orion bridge".

# The Orion node this board publishes as. Unset means node.local.
#ORION_NODE_ID=node.local

# The comm core to publish to, as Orion writes an address. Unset means the board's own comm core.
#ORION_ADDRESS=

# lemnosd's socket. The daemon makes it in its runtime directory, /run/lemnos.
#LEMNOSD_SOCKET=/run/lemnos/lemnosd.sock

# The identity the bridge drops to after it starts as root: the `lemnos-orion` user from lemnos.conf.
LEMNOS_ORION_USER=lemnos-orion
LEMNOS_ORION_GROUP=lemnos-orion
# Supplementary groups, comma-separated: lemnos (lemnosd's socket and the slot's .incoming directory)
# and the Orion node's group. The image sets the Orion node's group name. The example uses `orion`.
LEMNOS_ORION_GROUPS=lemnos,orion

# Devices that take files sent through Orion, and the directory each one's go into:
# device=/absolute/dir, comma separated. With systemd, add each directory to the unit's
# ReadWritePaths= in a drop-in. Unset means no device takes files.
#LEMNOS_ORION_FILES=slots=/data/slots/.incoming

# How long a caller may stay silent before its holds are released, in whole seconds. Unset means 60;
# 0 turns the lease off. A client that holds device state renews it with a request, a transfer chunk
# or a progress report before this runs out (`.call describe` renews with nothing else to do).
# See docs/daemon.md, "Leases".
#LEMNOS_ORION_LEASE=60

# The USB link: the gadget device (its id in the board file) whose bulk endpoints are offered to the
# comm core, and the link's name, which is the name on the first `interface` line of the gadget's
# composition (`orion-link` for the default composition). `lemnos-ctl tree BOARD --bridge-env FILE`
# writes this line from the board file; take it from there. The comm core must know a USB link by the
# same name. Unset means no link is offered, and the bridge says so once in its log. Several gadgets:
# comma-separated `device=link` pairs.
#LEMNOS_ORION_LINKS=gadget=orion-link
